%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: cea739211259f483da80de929a08eac2, type: 3}
  m_Name: LearnMoreBook
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::LearnMore.LearnMoreBook
  pages:
  - title: Home insurance
    subtitle: "What happens when your stuff gets damaged \u2014 and how insurance
      saves you."
    entries:
    - chapter: 1
      title: What is it?
      body: "Home insurance (hemf\xF6rs\xE4kring) covers your personal belongings
        \u2014 furniture, electronics, clothes and more \u2014 if they are damaged,
        destroyed or stolen. Without it, replacing everything comes straight out
        of your own pocket."
    - chapter: 1
      title: Damage that IS covered
      body: "\u2022 Fire, smoke and water damage\n\u2022 Theft and vandalism\n\u2022
        Accidental damage to electronics (e.g. dropped laptop)\n\u2022 Storm and
        natural disaster damage\n\u2022 Damage during a move (with moving insurance)"
    - chapter: 1
      title: Damage that is NOT covered
      body: "\u2022 Normal wear and tear\n\u2022 Damage caused on purpose\n\u2022
        Damage from serious neglect (e.g. leaving a window open in a storm)\n\u2022
        Items worth more than the policy limit (check your valuables cap)"
    - chapter: 1
      title: Your deductible
      body: "When you make a claim, you pay a small fixed part yourself \u2014 the
        deductible (sj\xE4lvrisk). The rest is covered by the insurer. Higher deductible
        = cheaper monthly fee, but more out-of-pocket when something breaks."
    - chapter: 2
      title: How to file a claim
      body: '1. Take photos of the damage right away.

        2. Find receipts or
        proof of what the item cost.

        3. Report theft or vandalism to the
        police first.

        4. Contact your insurance company and submit the claim.'
  - title: "Add-ons (Till\xE4gg)"
    subtitle: "What happens when the basics aren't enough \u2014 and how extra cover
      fills the gaps."
    entries:
    - chapter: 1
      title: What is it?
      body: "Add-ons are optional extras you attach to your basic hemf\xF6rs\xE4kring.
        The standard policy covers fire, theft and water damage \u2014 but not everyday
        accidents or high-value items. Add-ons extend the safety net to those gaps.
        You pick what you need and pay a little more each month."
    - chapter: 1
      title: Damage that IS covered
      body: "\u2022 <b>Drulle / allrisk</b> \u2014 sudden accidents: dropped phone,
        coffee spilled on laptop, broken glasses\n\u2022 <b>V\xE4rdesakf\xF6rs\xE4kring</b>
        \u2014 valuables above the standard cap: expensive laptops, jewellery, watches,
        cameras\n\u2022 <b>Extended travel cover</b> \u2014 trips longer than the
        standard 45 days\n\u2022 <b>Avbest\xE4llningsskydd</b> \u2014 cancelled or
        interrupted trips\n\u2022 <b>Bostadsr\xE4ttstill\xE4gg</b> \u2014 interior
        damage in a co-op flat (floors, kitchen, bathroom)\n\u2022 <b>All-risk outside
        the home</b> \u2014 accidental damage while travelling or at school"
    - chapter: 1
      title: Damage that is NOT covered
      body: "\u2022 Normal wear and tear\n\u2022 Technical faults or manufacturing
        defects (that's the manufacturer's warranty)\n\u2022 Carelessness \u2014
        e.g. leaving your laptop unattended in a caf\xE9\n\u2022 Damage you cause
        on purpose\n\u2022 Gradual damage, mould or rot\n\u2022 Your deductible \u2014
        it still applies to every claim"
    - chapter: 1
      title: Your deductible
      body: "Add-ons don't remove your deductible. You still pay the sj\xE4lvrisk
        (often around 1,000\u20131,500 SEK for accidental damage) each time you claim.
        A higher deductible lowers your monthly fee, but costs more when something
        actually breaks."
    - chapter: 1
      title: How to add them
      body: "1. Log in to Mina sidor and check what's already included \u2014 some
        policies bundle drulle automatically.\n2. Compare the add-ons against what
        you actually own (a new laptop? an expensive phone?).\n3. Add the extras
        you need and confirm the new price.\n4. Save your policy document \u2014
        f\xF6rs\xE4kringsvillkor \u2014 for your records."
